This is a review route, not an exhaustive module inventory. The writer in
`tools/handover/package.mjs` generates RUBY-MAP by scanning every selected
`src/**/*.ts` module for `.rb` references, explicitly retaining uncited modules.
It separately indexes divergence/unported/unsupported/deliberate-difference
annotations. Neither matching rule proves that all differences are known or
accepted. Review the shipped source and DIFFERENCES alongside that output.

The four acceptance categories remain persistence, semantics, rendering and
side effects. DSL/mod checks cross those categories rather than forming a
substitute score. Earlier source annotations, old comparison results and old
guide checkpoint claims retain their own source bindings; none is promoted to
acceptance of this integration or a later package. Required next step: bind the
final package/source/Ruby/checker/settings receipts listed in the companion
checklist, then independently review the complete generated map and package.
